THE SPRING RELEASE IS HERE

Hi Mara,

Midterms are coming, and so is a stack of first drafts. Our Spring
Release is built for exactly that moment: faster rubric setup, tighter
LMS sync, and new insight into how students actually use feedback.

Here's what's new.


--------------------------------------------------------------
1. RUBRIC PACKS
--------------------------------------------------------------

Start from a rubric your colleagues already trust. Rubric Packs are
ready-made, fully editable rubric sets for the assignments instructors
grade most:

  * Argumentative essay (first-year composition)
  * Lab report (introductory sciences)
  * Literature review (upper-division and graduate)
  * Reflective writing (practicum and clinical placements)
  * Annotated bibliography

Import a pack in two clicks, adjust criteria and point values to match
your syllabus, and share it across your department. Every comment
Scrivelo generates stays tied to a rubric criterion, so students can
see exactly where to focus their revision.

  >> Browse the Rubric Pack library: https://scrivelo.example/rubric-packs


--------------------------------------------------------------
2. LMS SYNC, REBUILT
--------------------------------------------------------------

We heard you: nobody wants to copy grades between tabs.

  * Two-way grade passback - rubric scores and instructor overrides
    flow back to the gradebook automatically.
  * Roster sync every 15 minutes (was hourly), so late adds and drops
    show up before the next submission window.
  * Assignment templates that carry your rubric, due dates and
    feedback settings from one term to the next.
  * Deep links from the LMS assignment straight into the feedback view.

Available now for all customers on our current integration. Your
campus administrator can switch it on under Settings > Integrations.


--------------------------------------------------------------
3. REVISION INSIGHTS (BETA)
--------------------------------------------------------------

Did the feedback land? Revision Insights shows instructors which
comments students opened, which ones they acted on in their next draft,
and where a whole section got stuck on the same criterion.

"Revision Insights told me in one glance that half my section didn't
understand what I meant by 'counterargument.' I re-taught it on
Tuesday." - Writing instructor, community college pilot

Join the beta: https://scrivelo.example/beta/revision-insights


--------------------------------------------------------------
ALSO IN THIS RELEASE
--------------------------------------------------------------

  * Comment bank search - find and reuse your own past comments
  * Spanish and French interface (more languages coming this summer)
  * Keyboard shortcuts throughout the feedback panel
  * Improved screen-reader labels on the rubric grid
  * Dark mode, because you asked. A lot.


